.Language=English,English
.PluginContents=System Parameters Editor
.Options CtrlColorChar=
@Contents
$ #System Parameters Editor#
  This plugin allows you to edit a lot of (i.e, currently over 20) parameters in Far manager
version 1.70 (and higher), which are not accessible through normal configuration.

  ~System Parameters, Page 1~@SystemSwitch1Params@
  ~System Parameters, Page 2~@SystemSwitch2Params@
  ~System Parameters, Page 3~@SystemSwitch3Params@
  ~System Parameters, Page 4~@SystemStringParams@
  ~Hot leys handling~@SystemHotKeyParams@
  ~XLat keys handling~@SystemXLatParams@
  ~Disabled options~@SystemDisableParams@

  #Contacting me:#
  #Pavel Kostromitinov#
  #2:5030/661.14@@Fidonet#
  #~kostrom@@mail.ru~@mailto:kostrom@@mail.ru@#

  Updates are available from ~my homepage~@http://lev.serebryakov.spb.ru/pavel/programs.shtml@.
  ~Vote~@http://www.uic.nnov.ru/~ruiv/plugring/cgi-bin/voter.cgi?ID=326@ for this plugin on PlugRinG!
See ~all my plugins~@http://www.uic.nnov.ru:8101/~ruiv/plugring/cgi-bin/downld.cgi?Draw=List&Select=Author&SelectAuthor=63@!

@SystemSwitch1Params
$ #System Parameters, Page 1#

  #Esc in Command-line history saves position# (TechInfo 9)
    If checked, pressing 3BEsc- while scrolling through command history with
3BCtrl+E--3BCtrl-X- keys, will save your position in history.

  #New 'Set Attributes' behaviour# (TechInfo 15)
    If checked, "Process subfolders" checkbox in "File Attrbutes"
dialog box will be unset for the single directory. Otherwise behavior will be
as in FAR prior to 1.70 version.

  #Show 'Debugger' button on exception# (TechInfo 17)
    If checked, button invoking default system debugger will be present in Exception dialog,

  #New Editor|Search behaviour# (TechInfo 18)
    If checked, the first search begins from the current position, the following
from the next position. Otherwise, search will work as in FAR prior to version 1.70.

  #Show drives hidden in Explorer# (TechInfo 30)
    If set, drives set to Hidden in explorer will be shown in Far anyway.

  #Show plugin name while testing file# (TechInfo 37)
    If set, names of plugin DLLs trying to open the file (e.g. archive or such) will be
shown in window title upon pressing 3BEnter- or 3BCtrl+PgDn-.

  #New console size switch scheme# (TechInfo 38)
    Use new window size changing mechanism (normal/maximal console size).

  #History positions on matching item# (TechInfo 41)
    If it is set, history in dialogs will position on item matching with entered text
upon opening it, otherwise - on the last (topmost) item.

  #Add plugin's prefix to path while copying to clipboard# (TechInfo 42)
    If set, upon adding a name of a file from plugin panel to clipboard (via 3BCtrl+Ins- or
3BCtrl+F-), it will be prefixed with a plugin's prefix.

  #Show scrollbar in menus# (TechInfo 43)
    Whether to show scrollbar in the menus that are too large.

  #Hidden attribute on hidden shares (Network plugin)# (TechInfo 35)
    Specifies whether Network plugin should set Hidden attribute while displaying
hidden shares.

  #Restore codepage after executing programs# (TechInfo 45)
    Use this to force Far to restore default codepage after running external programs.

  #Esc twice interrupts operation# (TechInfo 47)
    Allows to control the operation interruption behaviour. If set, pressing 3BEsc-
closes the message box and interrupts the operation, otherwise, operation is contiuned.

  #Case-sensitive filenames in history# (TechInfo 31, WinNT+ only)
    Whether to treat file names in viewer/editor history as case-sensitive.
   
  #Save configuration when console window is closed# (TechInfo 46, WinNT+ only)
    If this option set, Far tries to save its configuration (if auto-save is enabled)
when console window is closed via Close button in the window title bar.

@SystemSwitch2Params
$ #System Parameters, Page 2#

  #Right click in empty column# (TechInfo 6)
    Specifies action taken when right mouse buttn is clicked in an empty column.
    #Moves cursor and selects last file#
    #Moves cursor to last file#
    #Does nothing#

  #Editing Read-Only files# (TechInfo 19)
    Specifies handling of read-only files when opened for editing.
    #In read-only mode#          - open as if Ctrl-L was pressed after opening
    #Show warning message#       - warn of read-only file
    #Also with Hidden attribute# - apply the rules also to files with Hidden attribute
    #Also with System attribute# - apply the rules also to files with System attribute

  #URLs in help# (TechInfo 12)
    Specifies handling URL links in help files.
    #Disable# - URLs are not working
    #Enable#  - Default browser is launched
    #Prompt#  - A message appears
  #Alternative activation method#
    Try checking this, if URL activation doesn't work

@SystemSwitch3Params
$ #System Parameters, Page 3#

  #Show current character code in editor as# (TechInfo 32)
    Specifies radix to display current symbol code in editor
    #Octal#       - 3 digits, zero aligned
    #Decimal#     - 3 digits, space aligned
    #Hexadecimal# - 2 digits, zero aligned, 'h' appended

  #Show timing on copying# (TechInfo 26)
    Allows displaying information on average copying speed, copying time and average
remaining time.
    #To NUL#         - Enable when copying to NUL device ('read benchmarking')
    #Normal copying# - Enable on all other operations

  #SUBST drives query# (TechInfo 36, WinNT/2K only)
    Sets which drives should be tested if they're SUBST drives
    #Query removable drives#
    #Query other drives#

@SystemStringParams
$ #System String Parameters#

  #Template for personal plugins# (TechInfo 2)
    Specifies a template for personal plugins path. Environment variables
can be used here.

  #Word Dividers# (TechInfo 1)
    Specifies symbols that are treated as word dividers.

  #Word dividers for XLat# (TechInfo 16)
    Specifies symbols that are treated as word dividers when invoking XLat feature.

  #Editor/viewer bookmark cache# (TechInfo 11)
    Specifies the size of the cache used to save bookmarks of the editor/viewer.
The minimal value is 16, maximum is 128.

  #Maximal editor file size# (TechInfo 20)
    If file opened for editing is greater than specified size, a warning message
appears. If this value is 0, messages never appears.

  #Editor undo size# (TechInfo 44)
    Soecifies size of editor undo buffer. Can be any number from 64 up to 2 Gb,
though real buffer is limited by available memory

  #Size of buffer for copying# (TechInfo 23)
    Sets size (in bytes) of buffer to use while copying. Setting it to '0' enables
standard buffer of 0x10000 bytes.

  #Windowed cursor size# (TechInfo 25)
    Sets size (in percent) of insert and overwrite mode cursor when Far is in
windowed mode. Setting it to '0' allows using default console value.
  #Fullscreen cursor size# (TechInfo 25)
    Sets size (in percent) of insert and overwrite mode cursor when Far is in
fullscreen mode. Setting it to '0' allows using default console value.

  #Wipe symbol code# (TechInfo 29)
    Specifies symbol used in "Wipe file" operation (3BAlt+Del-)

  #Quoted symbols# (TechInfo 34)
    Specifies symbols, which will cause the filename containing them to be quoted
when needed.

  #Locale ID for sorting# (TechInfo 40)
    Sets which locale should Far use when comparing filenames.
    Special values are:
      0x0400 LOCALE_USER_DEFAULT
      0x0800 LOCALE_SYSTEM_DEFAULT
      0x0000 LOCALE_NEUTRAL
    For other values see <winnt.h>

  #Maximum files for panel auto-update# (TechInfo 41)
    Specifies maximum number of files on a panel with which auto-update works.
Set it to 0 to enable auto-update always.

  #Mouse wheel delta#           \
  #Mouse wheel delta in viewer#  (TechInfo 33, Win2000 only)
  #Mouse wheel delta in editor# /
    Specifies the number of keypresses of the 3BUp/Down- keys that are sent when
the mouse wheel is rotated and the keys 3BCtrl/Shift/Alt- are not pressed.
    Rotating the wheel when 3BShift- is pressed is equivalent to pressing 3BPgUp/PgDn-,
rotating the wheel when 3BAlt- is pressed always causes the scrolling by one position.

@SystemHotKeyParams
$ #Hot keys handling#
  
  #Ctrl-Alt-Shift works in# (TechInfo 7)
    Specifies where will this combination work.
    #File Panels# - hiding panels (see lower)
    #Editor#      - showing user screen
    #Viewer#      - showing user screen
    #Help Window# - hiding the window
    #Dialogs#     - hiding the dialog

  #Ctrl-Alt-Shift in panel hides# (TechInfo 8)
    Specifies exact behavior for 3BCtrl+Alt+Shift- in panels.
    #Panels only# - hide panels only, same as 3BCtrl+O-
    #Panels and command line# - hide command line also
    #Panels, command line and keybar# - hide everything, showing full user screen

  #BS clears 'unchanged' text# (TechInfo 5)
    If checked, pressing 3BBackSpace- in dialog input line, when it is in 'unchanged'
state, will clear the text (as 3BDel- key does); otherwise, it will remain.

  #BS deletes vertical block# (TechInfo 13)
    If checked, pressing 3BBackSpace- in editor with vertical block selected will delete it
the same as 3BDel- key does.

  #Ctrl+F adds name as shown# (TechInfo 14)
    If checked, pressing 3BCtrl+F- will add full current file name to command line
in the form it is displayed, otherwise in the original form.

  #New hotkey handling scheme# (TechInfo 21)
    Use layout-independent hotkey handling technique.
Helps when using "Janko's Keyboard Generator" or similar program, generating incorrect
.KBD files

  #New Shift/Ctrl/Alt handling scheme# (TechInfo 24)
    Use advanced method of handling shift keys and their combinations. E.g.,
3BAlt+NonLatinSymbol- will be treated as 3BAlt+LatinSymbol- (except that in quick search)

@SystemXLatParams
$ #XLat keys handling#

  #Key for Xlat in command line# (TechInfo 10)
  #Key for Xlat in dialogs#
  #Key for Xlat in editor#
    Specifies keys for Xlat feature. To enter a key, select appropriate input field
and press desired key combination.

  #Console detach key# (TechInfo 27)
    Specifies a key combination for detaching FAR Manager console from a non-interactive
process running in it.

@SystemDisableParams
$ #Disabled options (TechInfo 4)#
  This set of check boxes specifies different items in Options menu that are to be disabled.
